From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 00:24:42 -0400
Subject: thin the toolbar the rest of the way

The strip was 43 DIP and would not go lower by the location bar or the button
height, because a toolbar button is its icon plus its own padding and that
padding was the real floor. With it at 5 rather than 7, the strip is 39 -- down
from Chromium's 46.

It does not go below 39 by these constants: dropping the padding further, or the
margin with it, changes nothing, so something else floors it there. Left alone
rather than hunted down, since 39 is close to the reference and the next floor
is not obviously ours to move.

Why: the toolbar being visibly fatter than the reference was the first thing
noticed about it.
Removable when: the toolbar's metrics are themable.
---
 chrome/browser/ui/layout_constants.cc    | 2 +-
 chrome/browser/ui/stedding_ui_metrics.cc | 3 +++
 chrome/browser/ui/stedding_ui_metrics.h  | 5 +++++
 3 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/layout_constants.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/layout_constants.cc
index a8429ed9bd754..f9909a4e4be54 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/layout_constants.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/layout_constants.cc
@@ -210,7 +210,7 @@ gfx::Insets GetLayoutInsets(LayoutInset inset) {
     }
 
     case TOOLBAR_BUTTON:
-      return gfx::Insets(touch_ui ? 12 : 7);
+      return gfx::Insets(touch_ui ? 12 : stedding::kToolbarButtonInset.Get());
 
     case BROWSER_APP_MENU_CHIP_PADDING:
       if (touch_ui) {
diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/stedding_ui_metrics.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/stedding_ui_metrics.cc
index 1cf3edeb6389a..7575595d0f7d4 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/stedding_ui_metrics.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/stedding_ui_metrics.cc
@@ -27,6 +27,9 @@ BASE_FEATURE_PARAM(int, kLocationBarHeight, &kArcStyleWindow,
 BASE_FEATURE_PARAM(int, kToolbarVerticalMargin, &kArcStyleWindow,
                    "toolbar_vertical_margin", 4);
 
+BASE_FEATURE_PARAM(int, kToolbarButtonInset, &kArcStyleWindow,
+                   "toolbar_button_inset", 5);
+
 BASE_FEATURE_PARAM(int, kToolbarButtonHeight, &kArcStyleWindow,
                    "toolbar_button_height", 28);
 
diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/stedding_ui_metrics.h b/chrome/browser/ui/stedding_ui_metrics.h
index 9862b9432a7cc..4e6b1fa9c13a7 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/stedding_ui_metrics.h
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/stedding_ui_metrics.h
@@ -44,6 +44,11 @@ BASE_DECLARE_FEATURE_PARAM(int, kLocationBarHeight);
 // Space above and below the toolbar's contents, in DIPs.
 BASE_DECLARE_FEATURE_PARAM(int, kToolbarVerticalMargin);
 
+// Padding inside a toolbar button, in DIPs. Together with the icon this is what
+// really floors the toolbar's height: the strip is as tall as its tallest
+// child, and a button is its icon plus this on each side.
+BASE_DECLARE_FEATURE_PARAM(int, kToolbarButtonInset);
+
 // Height of a toolbar button, in DIPs. This, not the location bar, is what
 // actually sets the toolbar's floor -- the strip is as tall as its tallest
 // child, and the back button is that child.
